Xbox USB support
================

The USB code drives both MCPX OHCI controllers, enumerates root and external
hubs, and supports control and interrupt transfers. Devices without a class
driver remain available through the generic device interface.

The XID driver supports standard Microsoft gamepads:

    Duke          type 0x01, subtype 0x01
    Controller S  type 0x01, subtype 0x02

Input reports include the digital controls, pressure-sensitive face buttons,
triggers, and signed stick axes. Both rumble motors are supported.

Unsupported hardware
--------------------

The USB implementation does not yet support bulk or isochronous transfers.
Consequently, Xbox Memory Units, USB mass storage, the Xbox Live Communicator,
and other audio devices are not supported. FATX and KOS block-device support
are also absent.

The following XID devices require separate drivers and public interfaces:

    DVD Movie Playback Kit receiver       type 0x03
    steering wheels                       subtype 0x10
    arcade sticks and compatible pads     subtype 0x20
    light guns                            subtype 0x50
    Steel Battalion controller            type 0x80

Karaoke microphones, HID devices, third-party adapters, and other
title-specific accessories are not supported. New XID drivers must select
devices by type, subtype, capabilities, and report sizes. Devices whose
controls differ from a Duke or Controller S must not use xbox_controller_t.
